[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "French Defence: Advance Variation"]
[Variation "Advance Variation, Greek Gift"]
[ECO "C02"]
[Character "tactical,sharp"]
[Risk "medium"]
[EarlyMate "white"]
[Tricks "trap,mate-threat"]
[Refutes "1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Ne7 4. Nf3 Nf5 5. Bd3 c5 6. dxc5 Bxc5 7. O-O Nc6 8. a3 Bb6 9. Re1 O-O 10. Nc3 Nfd4"]
[Themes "greek-gift,h7-sacrifice"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "for-us"]
[Opponent "10...Nfd4"]
[Start "1. e4 e6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 Ne7 4. Nf3 Nf5 5. Bd3 c5 6. dxc5 Bxc5 7. O-O Nc6 8. a3 Bb6 9. Re1 O-O 10. Nc3"]

10... Nfd4 $2 { Black moves the knight from f5. Now nothing guards h7 but the king, and our queen can join the attack. } 11. Bxh7+ $1 { The Greek gift: give the bishop to drag the king onto h7. } 11... Kxh7 12. Ng5+ { Check from the knight, and it also opens the way for the queen. } 12... Kg6 ( 12... Kg8 13. Qh5 { Threatens Qh7 mate. Black has no good answer. } ) 13. Qd3+ { Another check; the king has no safe square. } 13... Nf5 14. g4 { Attacks the knight, which is Black's only defender, and opens a path for the queen to h3 or h5. } 14... f6 15. gxf5+ exf5 16. exf6 gxf6 17. Nf3 { White has two pawns and an attack for the bishop; Black's king is exposed and the pieces are about to join in. } *
